"process":"This is an automatically computed formula field in the 🔷⚡💟Individuals Sync table. It’s filled by the formula at record-evaluation time and is used downstream to drive scheduling/filters/automations in the ARCHR Eligibility workflow that need a numeric alert day (e.g., selecting records for reminders or aligning eligibility checks to calendar days)."},{
  "purpose": "Determines whether an \"Alert Due?\" flag is TRUE for an individual during the Individuals Sync by evaluating three automatic conditions: the record's sync mode equals \"In real time\", a specific required flag/field is empty/false, or a timestamp comparison between two date fields indicates the scheduled/compare timestamp is same-or-after the reference timestamp. The field is a formula (automatically computed) so it is not manually filled.",

